      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By the early 1900s, Stark hosted banks, a drugstore, lumber yards, and grain elevators operated by Benedict Grain and the Farmers Union.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
